lse,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118352","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118352","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118352.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118352.patch","merged_at":"2026-04-10T15:38:25Z"},"body":"~I'm not sure if this the Correct™ fix, but it solves the problem. For the theme context creation to work, it appears that the node must be visible when it happens. Whatever happened in #108647 made so that the `Theme` editor didn't count as \"visible\" anymore, and broke the mechanism.~\r\n\r\n~The actual source of the problem may be deeper than this. If so, I'm all ears for suggestions.~\r\n\r\nFound the actual problem: theme contexts get destroyed on node removal, and after #108647, `EditorDockManager::_move_dock()` gets called after the default theme preview gets ready, and since the ready state only happens once, it never gets re-created again.\r\n\r\nThis PR changes the notification to `NOTIFICATION_POST_ENTER_TREE`, which can be triggered indefinitely.\r\n\r\nFixes #116118.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","ty